{
  "_comment": [
    "docs/EMULATOR-COVERAGE.md's operation rows, one per callback method.",
    "This is the input to tools/coverage.nim and the only hand-maintained half of",
    "that document's headline. The demand side (which operations exist) is checked",
    "against reference/spt-4.1-surface.txt: every Callbacks method there must have",
    "exactly one row here and every row must name a method that is there. The",
    "supply side (what the emulator answers) is checked against the code: every",
    "route named here must be registered in mods/tarkov/tarkov.nim, every action",
    "named here must appear as a string literal in mods/tarkov/emu/*.nim, and every",
    "registered route must be named by some row.",
    "",
    "The bucket is NOT stored. It is derived: an operation with no route and no",
    "action is *not served*; one whose every route is bound to a stock stub handler",
    "(onNullData, onEmptyObject, onEmptyArray, onTrue) and which names no action is",
    "*served, deliberately empty*; everything else is *served and shaped*. That is",
    "why the three-bucket split can no longer drift away from the code.",
    "post1OnlyRoutes: routes the post-1.0 client asks for that have NO SPT 4.1",
    "Callbacks method behind them, so they cannot have an operations row --",
    "the demand side of this document is derived from that surface. They are",
    "still checked: every entry must be a route tarkov.nim really registers."
  ],
